  "practice": [
    "Say আ three times with an open, steady sound like the a in father: a, a, a.",
    "Read the common vocabulary aloud and listen for আ at the beginning of words.",
    "Practice the vowel sign: ক + া = কা, ম + া = মা, and ব + া = বা.",
    "Contrast অ (ô) with আ (a): অল্প (ôlpo), আম (am)."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "আ is the second independent vowel in the Bengali alphabet. It has an open a/ah sound similar to the vowel in father.",
    "After a consonant, আ is written with the া vowel sign rather than as the independent letter: ক + া = কা.",
    "The া sign appears in many everyday words, including মা, বাবা, নাম, ভালো, and বাংলা.",
    "Keep আ distinct from the shorter inherent অ sound. Compare আম (am, mango) with অল্প (ôlpo, a little)."
  ]
